{"path":"numeric/mul_sat","title":"std::mul_sat","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>mul_sat","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/mul_sat","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes the saturating multiplication x × y. This operation (unlike built-in arithmetic operations on integers) behaves as-if it is a mathematical operation with an infinite range.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/numeric\">&lt;numeric&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T mul_sat<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T x, T y <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturation_arithmetic\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">saturating</a> multiplication <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x × y</span></code>. This operation (unlike built-in <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/operator_arithmetic#Overflows\">arithmetic operations on integers</a>) behaves as-if it is a mathematical operation with an <i>infinite</i> range. Let <code><i>q</i></code> denote the result of such operation.\nReturns:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code><i>q</i></code>, if <code><i>q</i></code> is representable as a value of type <code>T</code>. Otherwise,\n</li><li> the largest or smallest value of type <code>T</code>, whichever is closer to the <code><i>q</i></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<p>This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code>T</code> is an <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/types#Integer_types\">integer type</a>, that is: <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">signed</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">short</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>, an extended signed integer type, or an unsigned version of such types. In particular, <code>T</code> must not be (possibly cv-qualified) <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">wchar_t</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">char8_t</span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char16_t</span></span>, and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char32_t</span></span>, as these types are not intended for arithmetic.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x, y\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> integer values\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Saturated <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x × y</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unlike the built-in arithmetic operators on integers, the <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/implicit_conversion#Integral_promotion\">integral promotion</a> does not apply to the <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code> arguments.\n</p><p>If two arguments of different type are passed, the call fails to compile, i.e. the behavior relative to <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/template_argument_deduction\">template argument deduction</a> is the same as for <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/min\">std::min</a></span> or <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/max\">std::max</a></span>.\n</p><p>Most modern hardware architectures have efficient support for saturation arithmetic on SIMD vectors, including SSE2 for x86 and NEON for ARM.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_saturation_arithmetic\"><code>__cpp_lib_saturation_arithmetic</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/26#cpp_lib_saturation_arithmetic_202311L\"><code>202311L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++26)</span></td>\n<td>Saturation arithmetic\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<p>See <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/tree/master/libstdc%2B%2B-v3/include/bits/sat_arith.h#L42\" data-external=\"1\">libstdc++ (gcc)</a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>Can be previewed on <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://godbolt.org/z/T58GEKPM6\" data-external=\"1\">Compiler Explorer</a>.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;climits&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;numeric&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\nstatic_assert\n<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// not saturated</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw405\">INT_MAX</span></a> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw405\">INT_MAX</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// saturated</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// not saturated</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw400\">INT_MIN</span></a> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw400\">INT_MIN</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// saturated</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// not saturated</span>\n    <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">mul_sat</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw410\">UINT_MAX</span></a> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw410\">UINT_MAX</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// saturated</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/add_sat\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>add_sat</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  saturating addition operation on two integers <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/sub_sat\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sub_sat</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  saturating subtraction operation on two integers <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/div_sat\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>div_sat</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  saturating division operation on two integers <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/saturate_cast\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>saturate_cast</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an integer value clamped to the range of another integer type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/clamp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clamp</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  clamps a value between a pair of boundary values <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/in_range\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>in_range</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if an integer value is in the range of a given integer type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/min\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>min</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the smallest finite value of the given non-floating-point type, or the smallest positive normal value of the given floating-point type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::numeric_limits&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/max\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>max</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the largest finite value of the given type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::numeric_limits&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"External_links\">External links</h3>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td>1.&nbsp;</td>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://locklessinc.com/articles/sat_arithmetic/\" data-external=\"1\">A branch-free implementation of saturation arithmetic</a> — Locklessinc.com, 2012\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2.&nbsp;</td>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XNMnQOFrEIY\" data-external=\"1\">C++ Weekly - Ep 459 - C++26's Saturating Math Operations</a> — Youtube.com, 2024-12-16\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"},{"depth":3,"text":"External links","id":"External_links"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::mul_sat","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++26. Computes the saturating multiplication x × y."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x, y"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Saturated x × y."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unlike the built-in arithmetic operators on integers, the integral promotion does not apply to the x and y arguments."},{"label":"Possible implementation","note":"See libstdc++ (gcc)."},{"label":"Example","note":"Can be previewed on Compiler Explorer."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"add_sat","note":"saturating addition operation on two integers"},{"label":"sub_sat","note":"saturating subtraction operation on two integers"},{"label":"div_sat","note":"saturating division operation on two integers"},{"label":"saturate_cast","note":"returns an integer value clamped to the range of another integer type"},{"label":"clamp","note":"clamps a value between a pair of boundary values"},{"label":"+3 more"}]}]},"standards":["C++17","C++20","C++26"],"wordCount":444,"codeBlockCount":1}
